<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE components PUBLIC "-//DBFLUTE//DTD LastaDi 1.0//EN"
	"http://dbflute.org/meta/lastadi10.dtd">
<components>
	<!-- Storage client components are provided by fess-storage-* plugins via fess_storage++.xml.
	     StorageClientFactory resolves them as "<storage.type>StorageClient", and the ++ suffix
	     merges into this file, so it stays even though core registers nothing of its own: without
	     a base file the plugins have nowhere to contribute to.

	     Keeping the storage.type-to-class mapping in the DI definition rather than in Java is what
	     makes that work. Setting storage.type to a component's name is enough to reach it, so a
	     plugin needs no change here to be reachable, and one plugin can register several names for
	     the same class: fess-storage-s3 serves both s3 and s3_compat, the auto-detection result for
	     MinIO and the like, that way. A storage.type whose plugin is not installed is a
	     configuration error the factory reports rather than a missing class.

	     The components are prototypes, not singletons: every caller takes the client in a
	     try-with-resources and closes it, which would shut down a shared instance. -->
</components>
